package dbguild

import (
	"bytes"
	"encoding/json"

	"go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2/bson"
)

// This file mirrors the `DBModuleMusic` family in
// `libraries/library-shared/src/db/schemas/DBGuildSchemas.ts`. The field
// ORDER of `ModuleMusic` matches the zod object schema in
// `apis/api-db/src/domain/zod-schemas/mongo/guild-schema.ts`
// (`moduleMusicSchema`) — the Node GET response is produced by
// `moduleMusicMigrationSchema.parse(...)`, which normalises key order to the
// schema-definition order, so matching that order keeps the JSON body
// byte-for-byte identical. Notably `commands_global` + `commands` sit BETWEEN
// `enhanced_search` and `text_channels` (where the removed `blocked_commands`
// used to live).
//
// SCHEMA v5 ("command access"): Node replaced the flat `blocked_commands:
// string[]` with the rich per-command access model shared with tempvoice —
// `commands_global` (DBCommandAccess) + `commands` (map keyed by slash name).
// The `dj` block is UNCHANGED and stays. The v5 zod preprocess migrates an old
// doc on read: `blocked_commands → commands[cmd].enabled=false`. See
// `MigrateMusicRaw`.
//
// Music's per-command `use_global` is the PER-AXIS object `{roles, channels,
// categories}` (Node commit b4f57ff switched it from a bare boolean; the
// version constant stayed 5), IDENTICAL in shape to tempvoice's
// `DBTempVoiceCommand`. The types are defined locally (not shared with
// tempvoice) to keep the verticals decoupled, matching moderation/modmail.

// MusicLoop mirrors the TS `DBMusicLoop` enum. JSON values are the lowercase
// strings — keep them in sync with `libraries/library-shared/src/db/schemas/DBGuildSchemas.ts`.
type MusicLoop string

const (
	MusicLoopNone  MusicLoop = "none"
	MusicLoopSong  MusicLoop = "song"
	MusicLoopQueue MusicLoop = "queue"
)

// MusicAudioQuality mirrors the TS `DBMusicAudioQuality` enum (schema v7).
// "hifi" asks api-music for FLAC (`/file/:id?format=flac`); it only takes
// effect for premium guilds and behind music-module's MUSIC_HIFI_ENABLED
// deploy flag. JSON values are the lowercase strings — keep in sync with
// `libraries/library-shared/src/db/schemas/DBGuildSchemas.ts`.
type MusicAudioQuality string

const (
	MusicAudioQualityDefault MusicAudioQuality = "default"
	MusicAudioQualityHifi    MusicAudioQuality = "hifi"
)

// VolumeDefaults mirrors the TS `DBVolumeDefaults` constant. Kept here for
// callers that want the same baselines without round-tripping through Mongo.
const (
	VolumeDefault = 40
	VolumeMin     = 0
	VolumeMax     = 100
)

// RadioMode tracks the "24/7 stay-in-channel" toggle (legacy-named "radio").
// `channel_id` is empty when disabled; never null in the Node service.
type RadioMode struct {
	Enabled   bool   `bson:"enabled"    json:"enabled"`
	ChannelID string `bson:"channel_id" json:"channel_id"`
}

// RadioModeGuild is one row of "which guilds of this bot have 24/7 on, and in
// which channel".
//
// It exists because there was no way to ask that question. The music module
// rebuilds players at boot from a Redis set of guilds that HAD a live player,
// so a 24/7 guild whose player was lost (node restart, session teardown, or the
// long-lived bug that let the idle timer collect persistent players) never came
// back on its own — Mongo still said "stay in channel X" and nobody ever read
// it. Asking guild-by-guild would be thousands of requests per boot.
//
// Declared here, in the shared domain package, so the `mongorepo` interface and
// the `mongo` implementation name the SAME type: those two packages duplicate
// their envelope types deliberately and only line up structurally.
type RadioModeGuild struct {
	GuildID   string `bson:"guild_id"   json:"guild_id"`
	ChannelID string `bson:"channel_id" json:"channel_id"`
}

// ChannelsConfig captures the include/exclude list used by both text and
// voice channel filters. `Exclude=true` flips the list semantics from
// "only these channels" to "every channel except these".
//
// `ShowAllowedChannels` hace que el módulo, al rechazar un comando por esta
// regla, añada al aviso la lista de canales donde SÍ se puede usar el bot.
// No necesita migración: el default es `false` y coincide con el valor cero de
// Go, así que un documento antiguo sin la clave se decodifica ya apagado.
type ChannelsConfig struct {
	Exclude             bool     `bson:"exclude"               json:"exclude"`
	ChannelsID          []string `bson:"channels_id"           json:"channels_id"`
	ShowAllowedChannels bool     `bson:"show_allowed_channels" json:"show_allowed_channels"`
}

// DJ holds the DJ subsystem flags. `Vote=true` enables consensus voting on
// queue-affecting commands; `Vote=false` falls back to "must have a DJ role".
// `Enabled=false` short-circuits the entire subsystem — bypasses included.
type DJ struct {
	Enabled     bool     `bson:"enabled"      json:"enabled"`
	Roles       []string `bson:"roles"        json:"roles"`
	Commands    []string `bson:"commands"     json:"commands"`
	Vote        bool     `bson:"vote"         json:"vote"`
	VoteTimeout int      `bson:"vote_timeout" json:"vote_timeout"`
}

// MusicAccessMode mirrors `DBAccessMode` (`"only" | "all_except"`) — the mode
// of a command access list. `only` = allowlist, `all_except` = denylist.
type MusicAccessMode string

const (
	MusicAccessOnly      MusicAccessMode = "only"
	MusicAccessAllExcept MusicAccessMode = "all_except"

